hadiths[62]{hadithnumber,text}:
"894","Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has ordered us to visit the sick, to follow the funeral (of a dead believer), respond to the sneezer (i.e., by saying to him: Yarhamuk-Allah after he says: Al-hamdu lillah), to fulfill vows, to help the oppressed, to accept the invitation extended by the inviter; and to promote greetings (i.e., saying As-Salamu `Alaikum). [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"895","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Every Muslim has five rights over another Muslim (i.e."," he has to perform five duties for another Muslim): to return the greetings"," to visit the sick"," to accompany funeral processions"," to accept an invitation"," to respond to the sneezer [i.e."," to say: 'Yarhamuk-Allah (may Allah bestow His Mercy on you)","' when the sneezer praises Allah] .\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"896","On his authority, he said that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “On the authority of Allah Almighty, the Most High, saying on the Day of Resurrection: ‘O son of Adam, I fell ill and you did not visit Me!’ He said: ‘O Lord, how can I visit You when You are the Lord of the worlds?’ He said: ‘Did you not know that such-and-such servant of Mine was sick and you did not visit him? Did you not know that had you visited him you would have found Me with him? O son of Adam, I asked you for food but you did not feed Me!’ He said: O Lord, how can I feed You when You are the Lord of the worlds?! He said: Did you not know that so-and-so servant of Mine asked you for food but you did not feed him, and did you not know that if you had fed him you would have found that with Me? O son of Adam, I asked you for drink but you did not give Me drink! He said: O Lord, how can I provide you with food when you are Lord of the worlds?! He said: So-and-so servant of Mine asked you for drink but you did not give him drink! Did you not know that if you had given him drink you would have found that with Me?” [Muslim]."
"897","On the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Visit the sick, feed the hungry, and relieve the suffering” [Al-Bukhari]."
"898","On the authority of Thawban, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) he said: “If a Muslim visits his Muslim brother, he will remain in the reward of the fruit of Paradise until he returns.” It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the desolation of Paradise? He said: 'It is its fruit.' [narrated by Muslim]."
"899","On the authority of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “There is no Muslim who visits a Muslim in the morning except that seventy thousand angels pray over him until the evening, and if he visits him in the evening except that seventy thousand angels pray over him until the morning, and he will have a share of the harvest fruits of Paradise” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"900","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A Jewish boy was serving the Prophet (ﷺ). He fell ill, so the Prophet (ﷺ) may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him, came to visit him. He sat at his head and said to him: “Islamic?” He looked at his father who was with him, so his father said: 'Obey Abu al-Qasim,' so he became Muslim. So the Prophet (ﷺ) came out saying: 'Praise be to Allah who saved him from the Fire.' [Al-Bukhari]."
"901","When a person complained to the Prophet (ﷺ) about an ailment or suffered from a sore or a wound, the Prophet (ﷺ) would gesture with his forefinger as shown, and Sufyan bin `Uyainah, the narrator, placed his forefinger on the ground then raised it (to demonstrate this gesture) and would recite: `Bismil-lahi, turbatu ardina, biriqati ba`dina, yushfa bihi saqimuni, bi 'idhni Rabbina' (With the Name of Allah, the dust of our ground mixed with the saliva of some of us would cure our patient with the permission of our Rubb.'' [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."
"902","When the Prophet (ﷺ) visited any ailing member of his family, he would touch the sick person with his right hand and would supplicate: \Allahumma Rabban-nasi"," adhhibil-ba'sa"," washfi"," Antash-Shafi"," la shifa'a illa shifa'uka"," shifaan la yughadiru saqaman [O Allah! the Rubb of mankind! Remove this disease and cure (him or her)! You are the Great Curer. There is no cure but through You"," which leaves behind no disease] .\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"903","And on the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said to Thabit, may Allah have mercy on him: Shall I not perform ruqyah for you with the ruqyah (healing supplication) of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)? He said: Yes, he said: Oh Allah, Lord of people, the healer of affliction, heal You are the healer, there is no healer but You, a cure that leaves no ailment” [Al-Bukhari]."
"904","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) visited me during my illness and supplicated, \O Allah! Cure Sa'd. O Allah! Cure Sa'd. O' Allah! Cure Sa'd.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"905","On the authority of Abu Abdullah Othman bin Abi Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, that he complained to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about a pain he found in his body, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, “Put your hand on the part of your body that hurts and say: In the name of Allah - three times - and say seven times: I seek refuge in Allah’s glory and power from the evil of what I find and what I fear” [Muslim]."
"906","And on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) (ﷺ) he said: “Whoever visits a sick person whose death has not arrived, and says to him seven times: I ask Allah Almighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you: then Allah will cure him of that illness” ([Abu Dawud].."
"907","And on his authority, the Prophet (ﷺ) (ﷺ) entered upon a Bedouin to visit him, and when he would enter upon a sick person to visit them, he would say: “There is no problem, purify yourself, Allah willing” [Al-Bukhari]."
"908","Jibril (Gabriel) came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \O Muhammad (ﷺ)! Do you feel sick?\"" He (ﷺ) said"," \""Yes.\"" Jibril supplicated thus (i.e."," he performed Ruqyah): \""Bismillahi arqika"," min kulli shay'in yu'dhika"," min sharri kulli nafsin aw 'ayni hasidi"," Allahu yashfika"," bismillahi arqika. [With the Name of Allah. I recite over you (to cleanse you) from all that troubles you"," and from every harmful mischief and from the evil of the eyes of an envier. Allah will cure you; and with the Name of Allah"," I recite over you] .\"" [Muslim] ."""
"909","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri and Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with them, that they bore witness against the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he said: “Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is great, his Lord has believed him, and he said: There is no god but me, and I am great. There is no god but Allah, to whom belongs the kingdom and to whom is praise. He said: There is no god but I, to me belongs the kingdom and to me is praise. And if he said: There is no god but Allah and there is no power nor strength except with Allah, he said: There is no god but me and there is no power nor strength except with Me. He used to say: “Whoever says it during his illness and then dies, the Fire will not feed him” [Al-Tirmidhi]"
"910","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, left the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during the illness in which the Prophet (ﷺ) died, and the people said: O Abu Al-Hasan, how is the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) this morning? He said: He has recovered, praise be to Allah. [Al-Bukhari]."
"911","While the Prophet (ﷺ) was reclining against me (during his last illness) I heard him saying: \Allahumma-ghfir li"," warhamni"," wa alhiqni bir Rafiqil-A`la (O Allah"," forgive me"," bestow Your Mercy on me and let me join with the exalted companions.'' [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"912","On her authority, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was dying, with a cup of water in it, and he put his hand into the cup, then wiped his face with water, then said: “O Allah, help me in the depths of death and the agony of death” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"913","On the authority of Imran bin Al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a woman from Juhayna came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him, while she was pregnant as a result of adultery, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed an offense that carries a prescribed (hadd) punishment, so impose the prescribed punishment on me. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called her guardian and said: “Be kind to her, and if she gives birth, bring her to me.” So he did, and the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered her to do so. He, may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him, and may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him, so she pulled her clothes over her, then he ordered her to be stoned, then he prayed over her” [Muslim]."
"914","On the authority of Ibn Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (ﷺ) and may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him, and he was feeling unwell, so I touched him and said: You are very unwell. He said: “I am feeling unwell as two men among you are feeling unwell.” (Agreed upon)"
"915","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to visit me when I had a severe pain. I said: \I am suffering from such trouble as you are observing. I am a wealthy man and the only heir of mine is my daughter.\"" (Then Sa'd narrated the whole incident). [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"916","\Oh"," my head.\"" (It was hurting due to pain.) Thereupon the Prophet (ﷺ) said"," \""Rather it is I who says: 'Oh"," my headache.\""' (Then Al-Qasim narrated the complete narration). [Al- Bukhari] ."""
"917","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \He whose last words are: `La ilaha illallah' (There is no true god except Allah) will enter Jannah.'' [Abu Dawud] ."""
"918","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Prompt your dying (ones) to say: There is no god but Allah” [Muslim]."
"919","On the authority of Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon Abu Salamah while his eyesight was dimming (as death approached), so he closed his eyes, then he said: “When the soul is seized, the sight follows.” Some of his family members started wailing in grief, and he said: “Do not pray for yourselves for anything but good, for the angels believe in what you say.” Then he said: “O Allah, forgive Abu Salamah, and raise his rank among the guided ones, and grant him a good successor among his descendants and those who come after him, and forgive us and him, O Lord of the Worlds, and make room for him in his grave, and light for him in it” [Muslim]."
"920","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \When you visit a sick or a dying person"," you should utter good words because the angels say `Amin' at what you say.'' She added: When Abu Salamah (May Allah be pleased with him) died"," I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," Abu Salamah has died.\"" He (ﷺ) directed me to supplicate thus: \""Allahummaghfir li wa lahu"," wa a`qibni minhu `uqba hasanatan [O Allah"," forgive me and him"," and grant me a good substitute in his place (give me a better replacement)].\"" So I supplicated as he directed"," and Allah gave me a man who was better for me than Abu Salamah (i.e."," the Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ)). (The Prophet (ﷺ) married Umm Salamah afterwards.) [Muslim] ."""
"921","On her authority, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “There is no servant who is afflicted with a calamity, and he says, ‘Indeed, to Allah, and to Him we shall return: O Allah, reward me for my calamity, and give me something better than it.’ Except that Allah Almighty will reward him for his calamity, and give him something better than it.” She said: When Abu Salamah died, I said as the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded me, so Allah replaced him with something better than him—the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).” [Muslim]."
"922","On the authority of Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: If a servant’s son dies, Allah Almighty says to his angels: You have taken my servant’s son, and they say: Yes. He says: You have taken the fruit of his heart, and they say: Yes. He says: What did my servant say? They say: He praised You and sought patience. Then Allah Almighty says: Build for my servant a house in Paradise, and name it the House of Praise.” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"923","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Allah Almighty says: “There is no reward for my faithful servant with Me if I take away his chosen one from the people of this world, and he seeks reward, his reward is nothing but Paradise” [Al-Bukhari]."
"924","A daughter of the Prophet (ﷺ) sent a message to him that her son was at his last breath, and requested him to come to her. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent back the informer saying: \To Allah belongs what He takes and what He gives"," and everything has a limited period (in this world). So ask her to endure patiently"," and expect the reward of Allah.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"925","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) visited Sa'd bin 'Ubadah during his illness. He was accompanied by 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Auf, Sa'd bin Abu Waqqas and 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud (May Allah be pleased with them). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) began to weep. When his Companions saw this, their tears also started flowing. He (ﷺ) said, \Do you not hear"," Allah does not punish for the shedding of tears or the grief of the heart"," but shows mercy by means of this (and he pointed to his tongue).\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"926","A grandson (child of the daughter) of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was presented to him while the child was at his last breath. Tears began to flow from the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Sa'd said to him: \What is this"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He (ﷺ) said"," \""It is mercy which Allah has placed in the hearts of his salves. Allah bestows His Mercy on the merciful among His slaves.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"927","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to his son Ibrahim (May Allah be pleased with him) when he was breathing his last. The eyes of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) began shedding tears. 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Auf (May Allah be pleased with him) said, \O Messenger of Allah"," you too weep?\"" He (ﷺ) said"," \""O Ibn 'Auf! It is mercy.\"" Then he began to weep and said"," \""The eyes are shedding tears and the heart is grieved"," and we will not say except what pleases our Rubb. O Ibrahim! Indeed we are grieved by your departure.\"" [Al-Bukhari] ."""
"928","On the authority of Abu Rafi’ Aslam, a servant of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Whoever washes a dead body and conceals it, Allah will forgive him forty times” [Narrated by Al-Hakim and he said it is authentic according to Muslim’s condition]."
"929","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Whoever follows the funeral procession and offers the funeral prayer for it"," will get a reward equal to one Qirat"," and whoever attends it till burial"," will get a reward equal to two Qirat.'' It was asked"," \""What are two Qirat?'' He (ﷺ) replied"," \""Equal to two huge mountains.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"930","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Whosoever attends the funeral of a Muslim believing and hoping for the reward from Allah and remains with it until the prayer is offered over it and the burial is completed"," he will return with a reward of two Qirat; each Qirat is equivalent to Mount Uhud; and whosoever offers his prayer over it and returns before its burial"," he will come back with one Qirat.\"" [Al- Bukhari] ."""
"931","On the authority of Umm Attiya, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: “We were forbidden from following funerals, and it was not imposed on us” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]. “And its meaning is” and he was not as strict in the prohibition as he was strict in the prohibitions."
"932","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \If a group of Muslims numbering a hundred perform funeral prayer over a dead person"," and all of them intercede for him"," their intercession for him will be accepted.\"" [Muslim] ."""
"933","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: “There is no Muslim man who dies and forty men who do not associate anything with Allah stand up for his funeral except that Allah will accept their intercession for him (the deceased).” [Muslim]."
"934","When Malik bin Hubairah (May Allah be pleased with him) offered a funeral prayer and found a small number of participants, he would divide them into three rows and would say that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \If three rows of men offer funeral prayer over anyone"," his entry into Jannah will become certain.\"" [Abu Dawud and At- Tirmidhi] ."""
"935","On the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman bin Awf bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed for me at a funeral, so I memorized his supplication as he said: “O Allah, forgive him, have mercy on him, keep him well, pardon him, honor his abode, widen his entrance, wash it with water, ice, and hail, and purify it of sins, just as you cleanse a white garment of filth, and replace it with a better home than its home, and welcome.” Better than his family, and a better husband than his wife, and admit him to Paradise, and protect him from the torment of the grave and the torment of the Fire.” Until he wished that I was that dead person. [Muslim]."
"936","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, Abu Qatada, and Abu Ibrahim Al-Ashhali, on the authority of his father - and his father is a Companion - may Allah be pleased with them, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) and may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him, that he prayed over a funeral and said: “O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our young and our old, our males and our females, those of us who are present and those who are absent. He died from us, so he died in faith; O Allah, do not deprive us of his reward, and do not test us after him.” [Al-Tirmidhi] from the narration of Abu Hurairah and Abu Hurairah Sahih and Al-Ashhali, and narrated by Abu Dawud from the narration of Abu Hurairah and Abu Qatada. Al-Hakim said: The hadith of Abu Hurairah is authentic according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim. Al-Tirmidhi said: Al-Bukhari said: The most authentic narrations of this. The hadith is narrated by Al-Ashhali. Al-Bukhari said: The most authentic thing on the subject is the hadith of Awf bin Malik."
"937","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: “When you pray for the dead, pray sincerely for him” [Abu Dawud]."
"938","The Prophet (ﷺ) supplicated in course of funeral prayer: \Allahumma Anta Rabbuha"," wa Anta khalaqtaha"," wa Anta hadaytaha lil-Islam"," wa Anta qabadta ruhaha"," wa Anta a'lamu bisirriha wa 'alaniyyatiha"," ji'naka shufa'a'a lahu [if the dead person is a man"," or laha if the dead person is a woman] "," faghfir lahu [or laha"," if it is a woman] (O Allah"," You are its Rubb; You created it; You guided it to Islam; You have taken its life back and You know best its insight and outer condition. We have come as intercessors"," so forgive him).\"" [Abu Dawud] ."""
"939","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led the funeral prayer of a Muslim man in our presence, and I heard him saying \Allahumma inna [name of the dead person] fi dhimmatika wa habli jiwarika"," faqihi fitnatal- qabri; wa 'adhaban-Nari"," wa Anta ahlul-wafa'i wal-hamdi; Allahumma faghfir lahu warhamhu"," innaka Antal-Ghafur-ur-Rahim [If the dead person is a woman"," one can change hu in some words here with ha] [O Allah"," (so-and-so son of so-and-so) is in Your Protection and inside the surroundings of Your Refuge. Safeguard him from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the Hell. You keep Your Promise and You deserve to be praised. O Allah! Forgive him and be merciful to him. Indeed"," You are the Forgiving"," the Merciful] .\"" [Abu Dawud] ."""
"940","While offering the funeral prayer of one of his daughters, he recited four Takbir, and after the fourth Takbir he continued standing for a time equal to an interval between two Takbir, praying for her and seeking Allah's forgiveness for her.\ Then he said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to do so.\"" Another narration is: He (Abdullah) recited four Takbir and remained standing in prayer for some time till we thought that he would recite the fifth Takbir. Then he gave Salam on the right and on the left. When he turned aside"," we asked him about it. He replied: \""I would add nothing to what I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) doing","\"" or he said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to do so.\"" [Al-Hakim] ."""
"941","I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, \Hurry up with the dead body (for its burial)"," for if it is pious"," you are speeding it to goodness and if it is otherwise"," you are laying an evil off your necks.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"942","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) and may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him, used to say: “When the funeral is laid, and the men carry it on their necks, if the deceased is righteous, she says: Bring me forward, and if the deceased is not righteous, she says to her family: Oh, woe to her, where are you taking her? Everything hears her voice except man, and if man heard, he would be shocked.” ([Al-Bukhari].."
"943","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him, and may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him, he said: “The believer’s soul is attached to his debt until it is paid for” [Al-Tirmidhi]."
"944","When Talhah bin Al-Bara' (May Allah be pleased with him) fell ill, the Prophet (ﷺ) came to visit him and said, \Verily"," I think that Talhah is about to die. So inform me when he is dead and make haste (in burying him). Indeed"," it is improper for the corpse of a Muslim to be kept lying unburied among his family members.\"" [Abu Dawud] ."""
"945","We were accompanying a funeral procession in Baqi` Al-Gharqad (graveyard in Al-Madinah) when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) proceeded towards us and sat down. We sat around him. He had a small stick in his hand. He was bending down his head and scraping the ground with the stick. He said, \There is none among you but has a place assigned for him either in the Jannah or in the Hell.\"" The Companions said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," should we not depend upon what has been written for us (and give up doing good deeds)?'' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""Carry on doing good deeds. Every one will find it easy to do such deeds (as will lead him to his destined place) for which he has been created.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"946","After the burial of a dead man, the Prophet (ﷺ) would stand by the grave and say, \Ask Allah to forgive your brother and supplicate for him for steadfastness because he is being questioned (about his deeds) now.\"" [Abu Dawud] ."""
"947","And on the authority of Amr ibn al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: If you bury me, then stand around my grave as long as the roots can be slaughtered, and its flesh divided so that I may find peace with you, and know what I will return to the messengers of my Lord with. Well."
"948","A man said to the Prophet (ﷺ): \My mother has died suddenly. I think that if she were able to talk (alive) she would have given in Sadaqah (charity). So"," if I give Sadaqah now on her behalf"," will she get the reward?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""Yes (she will be rewarded for that).\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"949","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “If a person dies, his work ceases except for three: ongoing charity, knowledge that is benefited from (by others), or a righteous child who prays for him” [Muslim]."
"950","On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: They passed by a funeral, and they praised it well, and the Prophet (ﷺ) and (ﷺ) and (ﷺ) said: “It is obligatory.” Then they passed by another, and they praised it badly, and the Prophet (ﷺ) may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him, and (ﷺ) said: “It is obligatory,” so Omar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: What? Is it obligatory? He said: “This man you praised well, so Paradise was granted to him, and this man you praised evil, so Hellfire became obligatory for him. You are Allah’s martyrs on earth” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]."
"951","On the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, he said: I came to Medina and sat with Omar ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him. A funeral passed by them, and the deceased (owner of the funeral) was spoken well of. Omar said: It is confirmed (that he is destined for Paradise). Then he passed by another, and the deceased was spoken well of. Omar said: It is confirmed (that he is destined for Paradise). Then he passed by a third, and the deceased was spoken ill of. Omar said: It is confirmed (that he is destined for Paradise). Abu Al-Aswad said: So I said: What did you oblige, O Commander of the Faithful? He (Omar) said: I repeated what the Prophet (ﷺ) said, who said: “Any Muslim for whom four testify that he is well, Allah will admit him to Paradise. So we said: And three? He said: ‘And three.’ So we said: And two? He said: ‘And two.’ Then we did not ask him about the one.’ [Narrated by al-Bukhari]."
"952","The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said, \Any Muslim who loses three children before they reach the age of maturity"," will be granted Jannah by Allah"," the Exalted"," out of His Mercy for them.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
"953","On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “No Muslim for whom three of his children die will be touched by Hell except as a fulfillment of Allah’s oath of mercy.” [Al-Bukhari and Muslim]"
"954","On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the men have taken your hadith, so set aside for us a day on which we will come to you and teach us what Allah has taught you. He said: “Gather together on such-and-such day.” So they gathered, and the Prophet (ﷺ) came to them and taught them what Allah has taught him. Then he said: “There is no woman among you for whom three children predecease her, but they will be a shield for her from the Fire.” A woman said: And two? Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “And two” (Agreed upon)."
"955","Ibn `Umar (May Allah be pleased with them) reported: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and his Companions reached Al-Hijr, the dwellings of the Thamud people, he admonished his Companions (saying), \Do not enter upon these punished people unless you are weeping"," lest the punishment should befall you as it had befallen them.\"" [Al-Bukhari and Muslim] ."""
